{% extends "base.html.jinja" %}

{% block content %}
<section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 pt-24 pb-8 text-center">
    <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-gray-500">Private preview</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight">Free during preview. No surprise bill.</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-gray-600">Forest pricing is still being validated with design partners. Billing is not active, there is no SLA, and preview users will not be charged without a separate agreement and advance notice.</p>
</section>

<section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-12">
    <div class="p-8 border-2 border-gray-900 rounded-lg">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-4">
            <div>
                <h2 class="font-bold text-2xl">Private Preview</h2>
                <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-gray-500">Invite-only · $0 · No SLA</p>
            </div>
            <a href="mailto:contact@kjuulh.io?subject=Forest%20private%20preview" class="inline-flex px-4 py-2 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-md text-sm font-medium hover:bg-gray-800">
                Join waitlist
            </a>
        </div>
        <ul class="mt-8 grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3 text-sm">
            <li>Private release control plane</li>
            <li>Versioned component exchange</li>
            <li>Forest Runtime where enabled</li>
            <li>Customer-infrastructure providers</li>
            <li>Limits agreed during onboarding</li>
            <li>No charge during preview</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-center">How paid pricing is being designed</h2>
    <div class="mt-8 grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
        <div class="p-5 border border-gray-200 rounded-lg">
            <h3 class="font-bold">Platform subscription</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-600">The leading subscription metric counts an active human developer once per UTC month. It covers the release control plane, component exchange, policy, audit, and support.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-5 border border-gray-200 rounded-lg">
            <h3 class="font-bold">Forest Runtime</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-600">Managed application compute will use a separate transparent consumption meter with included credit, budget alerts, hard limits, and advance notice before overages.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-5 border border-gray-200 rounded-lg">
            <h3 class="font-bold">Your infrastructure</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-600">Provider work on customer-owned infrastructure is not billed as Forest compute. Customers still pay for the control plane, private artifacts, policy, audit, and support.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-12">
    <div class="p-6 border border-amber-200 bg-amber-50 rounded-lg">
        <h2 class="font-bold text-lg">Trusted preview environments only</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700">Forest Runtime and provider-backed releases exist, but neither carries a production hosting guarantee. Native components and release providers are trusted code, and runner, provider, artifact, workload, and tenant isolation require further hardening. Those controls are productization gates—not paid add-ons or shipped preview guarantees.</p>
    </div>
</section>
{% endblock %}
